/-!
# Programs for projective real klt threefolds

Let `g : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of projective complex varieties, with `X` a normal `ℚ`-factorial
threefold with canonical divisor `K`, and let `(X, B)` be a klt pair with effective real boundary
`B`. Then there is a finite `(K + B)`-program over `S` — a sequence of divisorial contractions of
`(K_i + B_i)`-negative extremal rays of `NE̅(X_i/S)` and of real flips of the small contractions
of such rays, the boundaries being the successive birational transforms — passing only through
projective `ℚ`-factorial real klt threefolds over `S`, whose last model `(X_n, B_n)` either has
`K_n + B_n` nef over `S` or admits the contraction over `S` of a `(K_n + B_n)`-negative extremal
ray of `NE̅(X_n/S)` which is of fibre type.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.IsRealKltPair.exists_program_isRelativelyNef_or_isFibreType`.

## Implementation notes

The program is spelled out as data indexed as in `MMP.Fourfold.RelativeDltProgram`: models
`X₀ = X`, `X_{i+1} = Yi i` over `S`, a number `n ∈ ℕ` of steps, and for `i < n` a
`(K_i + B_i)`-negative extremal ray `R_i` of `NE̅(X_i/S)` (negativity through
`MMP.Flips.IsRIntersectionNumber`) with its contraction `f_i : X_i ⟶ Z_i`, `h_i : Z_i ⟶ S`
over `S` (`MMP.Mori.IsRelativeContractionOfFace`, `MMP.Flips.IsNegativeExtremalContraction`),
followed by `f_i⁺ : X_{i+1} ⟶ Z_i` over `S` which is an isomorphism when `f_i` is divisorial and
a real flip (`MMP.Fourfold.IsRealFlipStep`) otherwise; in both cases
`B_{i+1} = (f_i⁺)⁻¹_* (f_i)_* B_i`. A contraction `X_n ⟶ Z` is of fibre type when
`dim Z < dim X_n`.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori]
-/

@[expose] public section

